Law School is really expensive and it's  easy to assume that the only good  resources in law school are also really  expensive but that's simply not the case  today we're gonna talk about the free  resources that you should be using to  supercharge your law school education  and get better grades the first free  resource that I would recommend in law  school is called Anki akhi is a digital  flashcard software simply put there is  no better way to help you memorize  things paper flashcards get a bad rap  and part of that is deserved but there's  been a lot of research into the science  of memorizing things over the last 20  years recently study after study has  shown that something called spaced  repetition learning can supercharge your  ability to recall things the basis of  the system is simple the more you  remember something the less you need to  study the less you remember it the more  often you need to see the flashcard unki  has this kind of period is a Schnoor  spaced repetition built into it it's  been used by language learners for years  it allows people to learn entire  languages in just months in fact I'm  using it to learn Japanese right now so  for example if I am displayed a  flashcard and I get the answer right  then I tell the software that I got that  card right and I won't see that a card  again for a day but if I got the card  wrong then I'll see that card again  within one minute I'll keep seeing it  until I get that card right this system  is the fastest way to remember things  like elements of a cause of action or  memorizing the facts of a particular  case if you use visual cues like  pictures or mnemonics you can really  supercharge your ability to learn these  concepts really fast not everything that  you need to learn for final exams is  conductive to being memorized via  flashcards like a key but I'd say that  at least 80% is if you want to memorize  things in the minimum amount of time use  Anki or another spaced repetition  flashcard system it is a great system  very few people use it and it is  perfectly free on a laptop the next free  resource that I would use is West law  West law is  not just the thing that you have to use  in your legal writing a research class  it's also a wonderful tool for short  cutting your study time lawyers are very  lazy they are willing to pay a ton of  money to have things spoon-fed to them  and Westlaw and LexisNexis fill that  need every American case is reported and  analyzed by an army of lawyers here at  legal eagle we recommend commercial  outlines and case summary services like  Quimby but you can get 90% of the  benefit of those things straight from  Westlaw itself they summarize the facts  and most importantly they give you the  black letter law find what works best  for you and your professor between  commercial supplements and outlines but  don't forget the Westhead notes as well  and read those first before you dive  into your case book it will make your  reading so much clearer save you  headaches and save you time we go into  this in more depth in our guide to law  school cases you can get a link to that  down below the third free resource you  should use is your law school librarian  your law school librarians can help you  with just about anything writing  assignments research assignments Law  Review articles just about anything but  the most important thing they can help  you with is practice tests unfortunately  law schools tend to keep a tight lid on  their practice tests so they make it  hard to find and they certainly don't  advertise them your law librarians are  the gatekeepers they are your best  resource for finding prior exams from  your school and most importantly for  your particular professor I talk about  practice exams a lot on this channel  it's one of the most important things  you can do to get better grades so go  get them from your law librarians get as  many as you can get exams from other  professors it doesn't matter just do  them your grades will thank you okay the  next free resource that I would  recommend in law school is Dropbox or  Google Drive some sort of cloud storage  system everyone has a horror story about  their laptop crashing the night before a  writing assignment is due or losing  their outline just before they started  studying all of your law school files  should be pretty small just Word  documents mainly so sign up for a free  Dropbox  Google Drive account automatically save  your work to those folders and while  you're at it tell word to autosave your  work every few seconds your peace of  mind is worth this free resource and  there's just no reason in this day and  age not to have some sort of cloud  system the next free resource I would  recommend is your school's gym it's too  easy to get completely out of shape in  law school thanks to the arms race  between colleges odds are you have  access to a really nice gym on campus  and that probably includes classes that  are free to take at the gym part of  doing well in law school is staying  mentally and physically fit so don't  neglect your gym and don't neglect your  body or your health as well it's too  easy to fall into the trap of eating  nothing but junk food and just studying  all the time but in the long run it is  better for you to stay mentally and  physically fit and that requires that  you go to the gym every once in a while  the next free resource you should  absolutely use in law school is your  professor you should go to office hours  it is amazing how few people actually go  to the professor's office hours these  people are experts in their field and  more importantly they are the ones that  are going to test you on your final exam  so find out what they in particular  think about a certain section of law  their version is more important than any  other resource if your professor  contradicts a commercial supplement go  with your professor that's the version  that's going to be on the test  but you can 